# No eyebrow/overline labels above titles

## Rule

- Do **not** add “eyebrow/overline” UI above headings (e.g., small uppercase labels like `On the record`, `In the news`, `News hub`, `Video` sitting above an `h1/h2`).
- Do **not** add decorative bullet/dot/marker/badge elements next to those labels (e.g., small gradient squares/dots used as a marker).

## Do instead

- Put the context **in the title** or **in the subhead**.
- If context is needed for scanning, use a **short subhead sentence** under the title (not an overline label).

## Examples

### Bad

- `On the record` (small label above the title)
- `In the news` (eyebrow above the title)
- Any dot/square/marker next to those labels

### Good

- Title: `Op-eds & commentary`
- Subhead: `Published commentary on the issues — direct, clear, and on the record.`

